2. pi — https://github.com/earendil-works/pi
================================================================================

Pinned at commit 8eb2bccf2603c28907ef3a583a04cafb1af284ae, the same pin five of
this repository's other package NOTICEs already use.
Upstream licence: MIT — Copyright (c) 2025 Mario Zechner, already retained in
this package's LICENSE.

Provenance: fork-and-adapt, not clean-room, and heavily adapted. This section is
weaker than section 1 and is labelled partial rather than asserted.

How far the audit behind this section actually goes:

  - Basename correspondence was established between this package's `src/` and
    `pi`'s `packages/agent/src/`, including the `harness/` subtree that holds
    most of the overlapping names.
  - Distinctive-line carry-over (lines >= 25 characters, excluding boilerplate)
    was then sampled on six file pairs, as a percentage of upstream's own
    distinctive lines:

        proxy.ts                                    63%
        compaction/messages.ts                      32%
        compaction/branch-summarization.ts          27%
        compaction/compaction.ts                   23%
        agent-loop.ts                               23%

    These figures describe adaptation, not equality. Upstream's compaction and
    agent-loop modules have been substantially rewritten here, so this package
    is NOT byte-identical to upstream modulo formatting — the language used by
    the other package NOTICEs in this repository would overstate it here.
  - Six pairs out of this package's 43 source files were sampled. The remaining
    files have NOT been audited, and the samples are not claimed to be
    representative of them.

What this section does not claim: a per-file attribution list for the pi
derivation, and a definitive statement of which of this package's files derive
from pi at all. Both remain open work. Note that other pi packages
(`packages/ai`, `packages/tui`, `packages/coding-agent`) carry the same pi
derivation and the same absence of a NOTICE; this file does not speak for them.